---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons targets rm -h <==
Forget a client

Usage: omaddons targets rm [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  The target's id

Options:
      --purge  Also delete what omaddons kept for it (an uninstalled client only)
      --yes    Confirm a purge: delete what its preview lists

Examples:
  omaddons targets rm warmane  forget it; its files stay
  omaddons targets rm classic --purge --dry-run
                               an uninstalled client: what a purge deletes
  omaddons targets rm classic --purge --yes --if-match <token>
                               delete exactly that preview

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons targets rm --help <==
Forget a client

Unregister it; nothing in its directory is touched. With --purge, a client that is no longer
installed also loses what omaddons kept for it.

Usage: omaddons targets rm [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The target's id

Options:
      --purge
          Also delete what omaddons kept for it (an uninstalled client only)
          
          Its Interface/.omaddons/ (WTF backups, undo snapshots, its marker), the state halves of
          its transactions and its record. It cannot be undone: preview it with --dry-run, then run
          it with --yes.

      --yes
          Confirm a purge: delete what its preview lists

Examples:
  omaddons targets rm warmane  forget it; its files stay
  omaddons targets rm classic --purge --dry-run
                               an uninstalled client: what a purge deletes
  omaddons targets rm classic --purge --yes --if-match <token>
                               delete exactly that preview

See also: targets, backup list

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias:
                          --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Run only what the preview that returned this token showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
